1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,220
As new technology is introduced, there are many who worry about its impact on our current and future lifestyles – particularly when it comes to jobs.
随着新技术的引入，很多人担心它对我们当前和未来生活方式的影响——尤其是在工作方面。

2
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:22,490
It is a current belief that with the rise of robotics and artificial intelligence, many people’s jobs, and therefore their livelihoods, are likely to be lost to automation.
目前人们普遍认为，随着机器人技术和人工智能的兴起，许多人的工作，进而他们的生计，可能会因自动化（automation）而丧失。

3
00:00:22,490 --> 00:00:25,350
This type of fear isn’t new.
这种担忧并非新鲜事。

4
00:00:25,350 --> 00:00:35,140
In the 19th century, the automated weaving machine was revolutionising the English textiles industry and would contribute to the Industrial Revolution.
在19世纪，自动织布机彻底改变了英国的纺织业，并促成了工业革命。

5
00:00:35,140 --> 00:00:41,680
When manual workers became redundant, it sparked protests at the loss of their vocation.
当手工工人被裁员（redundant）时，就引发了人们对失去工作（vocation）的抗议。

6
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:45,680
Automation in the work place is nothing new.
工作场所的自动化并非新鲜事物。

7
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:55,830
Machines have been performing menial tasks on our behalf for years, allowing us to escape the drudgery that accompanies many repetitive jobs.
多年来，机器一直在替我们执行枯燥琐碎的（menial）任务，使我们得以摆脱许多重复性工作所带来的辛苦乏味的苦差事；单调乏味（drudgery）。

8
00:00:55,830 --> 00:01:06,390
In fact, the International Federation of Robotics states that in manufacturing on average there are now 74 robots per 10,000 employees.
事实上，国际机器人联合会指出，在制造业中，目前平均每10000名员工就有74台机器人。

9
00:01:06,390 --> 00:01:10,300
That has risen from 66 in 2015.
这一数字与2015年66台相比有所上升。

10
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:22,550
General Manager of Digital Customer Engagement Solutions at tech firm Nuance, Bernard Louvat, believes that ‘AI is a big threat to low-skilled jobs, no question.’
科技公司Nuance的数字客户互动解决方案总经理伯纳德・卢瓦特（Bernard Louvat）认为，“毫无疑问，人工智能对低技能工作来说是一个巨大威胁。”

11
00:01:22,550 --> 00:01:28,720
He also thinks that AI chatbots will oust most call centre staff within a decade.
他还认为，人工智能聊天机器人将在十年内取代（oust）大多数呼叫中心员工。

12
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:39,600
When you consider that a large telecoms company like AT&T employs around 100,000 call centre staff, that’s a lot of people on the dole.
当你想到像美国电话电报公司（AT&T）这样的大型电信公司雇佣了约10万名呼叫中心员工时，那就意味着会有很多人靠失业救济金生活。

13
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:42,180
And that’s just one industry.
而这只是一个行业。

14
00:01:42,180 --> 00:01:56,950
A recent report from the McKinsey Global Institute, a private sector think tank, states that nearly two thirds of all jobs could have at least 30% of their activities automated by 2030.
私营企业智库麦肯锡全球研究所（McKinsey Global Institute）最近的一份报告指出，到2030年，几乎三分之二的工作至少有30%的工作内容可以实现自动化。

15
00:01:56,950 --> 00:02:09,300
However, McKinsey also believes that this new technology will also ‘create new occupations that do not exist today, much as technologies in the past have done.’
然而，麦肯锡也认为，这项新技术也会“创造出如今尚不存在的新职业，就像过去的技术所做的那样”。

16
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:20,340
As the horse gave way to the car, hostlers became mechanics and mechanised manufacturing drove up wages and created more long-term roles than it destroyed.
随着马被汽车取代，马夫（hostlers）变成了机械师，机械化制造业提高了工资水平，创造出的长期岗位比它淘汰的岗位更多。

17
00:02:20,340 --> 00:02:33,680
In fact, figures from the World Bank have shown that despite a 2.2 billion rise in population between 1991 and 2017, global unemployment has fallen by 0.3%.
事实上，世界银行的数据显示，尽管1991年至2017年间人口增加了22亿，但全球失业率却下降了0.3%。

18
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:43,200
‘It’s an evolution of work’ says Ian Barkin, co-founder of Symphony Ventures, a robotic process automation specialist.
Symphony Ventures的联合创始人，机器人流程自动化专家伊恩・巴金（Ian Barkin）说：“这是工作的一种进化。”

19
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:49,020
As low-skilled jobs are taken on by AI, people will need to learn new skills.
随着人工智能承担低技能工作，人们将需要学习新技能。

20
00:02:49,020 --> 00:02:57,540
‘This calls on us to focus on up-skilling, Technology can lead to job reductions but it doesn’t have to,’ says Barkin.
巴金说：“这就要求我们专注于技能提升（up-skilling）。技术可能会导致工作岗位减少，但也并非必然如此。”

21
00:02:57,540 --> 00:03:03,040
Whether or not robotics and AI will leave us all jobless remains to be seen.
机器人技术和人工智能是否会让我们都失业还有待观察。

22
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:05,760
Current views on the subject are mixed.
目前关于这个问题的观点不一。

23
00:03:05,760 --> 00:03:15,560
Increased automation could indeed lead to a loss of some jobs, but at the same time is likely to create many more as new skills are required.
自动化程度的提高确实可能导致一些工作岗位的流失，但同时，由于需要新技能，也可能会创造出更多的岗位。

24
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:17,360
Will they balance out?
它们会达到平衡吗？

25
00:03:17,360 --> 00:03:21,140
I’ll get my AI assistant to get back to you on that one.
关于这一点，我会让我的人工智能助手再回复你。
